    "Practical part: the candidate's own machine with JDK 25, Apache Maven 3.9 or later and an IDE, plus the provided assessment project; the project runs fully offline after its one-time dependency setup, uses only an embedded in-memory H2 database, and needs no cloud account, container engine, AI service or shared hosted service.",
    "MCQ part: closed book, no external resources; the platform assessment owner enforces the resource rule in the delivery system."
  ],
  "instructions": "Spring Boot graded course final, distinct from all practice. It is platform-scheduled as its own timed sitting outside the frozen day templates; S13 only names where the course closes. Part 1 is a 150-minute practical: one coherent candidate-local Spring Boot 4.1.2 project (pulled to the candidate's machine like the module labs, graded by the platform owner against the submitted project) of about 8 linked tasks across layers, persistence, validation and errors, testing, the outbound client and security, checked locally with mvn -q -o test. Part 2 is a 40-item, 50-minute MCQ covering the taught predict-and-explain objectives. Both parts draw only on taught course content and are varied or modestly harder than the practice labs and mastery checks: same skills, fresh scenario and data, no reused practice items. Weights: practical 60, MCQ 40; pass mark 70% overall. This blueprint is deliberately value-free: it carries no items and no answer material, and the item banks, keys and scoring materials are authored only on the permitted private route, held by the platform assessment owner, and never enter this repository. Manual upload ownership is unchanged."
